<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadashivrao Bhau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1730–1761</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadashivrao Bhau was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> general and cousin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balaji-baji-rao">Balaji Baji Rao</a>. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a> at Udgir in 1760, gaining large territories, and then commanded the Maratha army against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a>. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat">Third Battle of Panipat</a> in 1761.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sadashivrao-bhau.jpg" alt="Sadashivrao Bhau" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Deccani School · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_portrait_in_an_oval_of_the_Bhao,_Sadhashir_Rao,.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
